"## Summary\n\nMembers follow-up 23: the D-098 archive of run `3eb3960d`, paired path and native-window instrumentation for F22-AT01 and F22-D146, and one assembled run on devstack 35's `main`, judged by unchanged predicates.\n- **Session:** launched 06:39 EST on 2026-11-04 on #468's roadmap row `c148cf34`, and delivered at 08:01.\n- **Model:** codex `gpt-6-astra`.\n- **Size:** 4 commits and 408 owned files, +1,480,372/−130,358. Almost all of it is records: the D-098 archive and the new run's records. The largest file is `AT09.json` at 12.96 MB, and the total added is 213 MB.\n- **Checks:**\n  - merge-tree clean on current `main`; prepush-scan clean, including the archive's gzip blob; owned-check passes.\n  - **The orchestrator reran these** on a scratch tree: `main` after isolation 23 (#469, `0f0cd11f`), with agent-core 51, updater 26, handover 45 and this branch merged in. Those three merge before this PR. All pass:\n    - `make -f mk/at-members.mk at-members-lint at-members-test at-members-build`: the area lint, `go test ./tests/e2e/at/members/...`, and the probe and fixture helpers built for linux amd64 and arm64;\n    - `go test -tags e2e ./tests/e2e/at/members/...`, and the lane's `underlay_evidence_test.py`;\n    - `make -f mk/e2e.mk e2e-lint`;\n    - `go vet ./...` and `go vet -tags e2e ./tests/e2e/...`;\n    - `go test ./tests/handover/...`;\n    - the committed-evidence tests (`TestCommitted*` in `tests/netlab`, `tests/e2e` and `tests/e2e/at/...`, including `TestCommittedEvidenceHygiene`);\n    - `make go-lint`, gofmt and `git diff --check`;\n    - `followup23_records.py` and `followup23_window_records.py`, which rebuilt every follow-up 23 index from the measured originals byte for byte, leaving the tree clean.\n- **Scope:** one assembled run in the lane's own namespace, with no retry and no reservation. Zero owned Docker objects at the end.\n  - **Admission waited 0 s.** 587 process samples, and no foreign process inside any acceptance envelope.\n  - **Its one foreign window,** six teardown samples at 12:43:49–12:44:14Z (pid 198676, `bash`), came after the acceptance command ended at 12:43:30.6Z. It is the merge queue's gates for isolation 23, which started at 12:43:41Z, when the timing hold released. The lane recorded it as confounded under D-133; it intersects no measured case.\n\n**The orchestrator's reading.**\n- **D-098 first** (`2d4d37a8`): run `3eb3960d`'s 122 root records are archived byte-identically, gzip blob unchanged, with SHA-256 pins. Every earlier archive and dated note is untouched, and 761 relative links resolve.\n- **The run:** `6a25221b` on harness `8bde2b6a`, baseline `c148cf34`, which is `main` after devstack 35 (#468). **3 pass, 7 blocked, 0 fail; 706 passed, 8 blocked and 0 failed subchecks.** Exit 2 because of the blocked rows.\n  - AT02, AT03 and AT08 pass. AT01, AT04, AT05, AT09, AT20, AT21 and AT22 are blocked.\n  - **Against run `3eb3960d`:** AT01's first transfer is counted again, so its four conditional continuation checks ran: 702 + 4 = 706. Every other case has the same counts. No predicate was removed, and every earlier run keeps its recorded outcome.\n  - **Merged since:** isolation 23 (#469) changed only `docs/`. Agent-core 51 and updater 26 merge ahead of this PR; the run measured neither.\n- **F22-D146 is located, and the orchestrator's reading in #467 was wrong on two points.**\n  - **The cadence:** the regular node's prepared config, `tests/e2e/cmd/fvpn-e2e-prepare/main.go` (`writeAgentConfigs`), sets `heartbeat_seconds` and `poll_seconds` to 5 but no `observation_seconds`. `node/agent/config.go` then defaults it to 30 s. The retained prepared config confirms the field is absent, and the new nine-row windows, which read every stored observation, show successive reports 30.015–30.019 s apart.\n  - **The bound:** the members serving query needs an observation under 15 s old (`received_at > clock_timestamp() - interval '15 seconds'`). So any single read finds a fresh enough observation during only about half of each 30 s period.\n  - **First correction:** #467 said the lab's agents report every 5 s, citing `tests/e2e/installer_fixture.go:119`. That override applies only to the installer node.\n  - **Second correction:** #467 read the 34.85 s between two retained latest rows as a gap in which control accepted no observation. Two latest rows cannot prove that, and the full windows show reports every 30 s.\n  - **This run:** IPv6 1280 indexes 49 and 51 now pass. Dual 1280 indexes 44 and 46 are blocked: the later read at 12:41:30.91Z finds generation 75 throughout, the current incarnation, forwarding enabled and no reasons, and its latest observation, received at 12:41:08.31Z, is **22.61 s old**. That is the only failed condition.\n  - **The 15 s bound is not a product rule.** It appears only in acceptance SQL: the members serving query, and devstack's follow-up 26 and 30 live tests.\n- **F22-AT01: the node's reply reached the member's underlay.**\n  - **Matched packets:** node packet 158, at 08:22:37.385050Z, and member packet 161, 9 µs later, have the same IP hash. The node's 140-byte IPv6 WireGuard response went out `eth2` and reached member `eth1`. Its source is the IPv6 loopback label `addr-eff8e7ca506627fe`, not the selected node endpoint.\n  - **Then it was lost:** member header errors rose from 0 to 1 while WireGuard receive bytes stayed at zero. The first unconfirmed boundary is after member underlay ingress and before WireGuard receive accounting.\n  - **Not proven:** there is no packet-specific kernel drop trace, and no source-selection mechanism is shown. The lane extracted this from the original capture receipts, `F23-retrospective-F22-AT01.json`, and the old outcome stands.\n  - **So the #467 reading, that none of the node's traffic reached the member, was too strong.** The member received it and dropped it.\n- **New first transfers:** AT01's initial and wake transfers and AT08's initial transfer are each counted by one origin receipt and both counters' increments. AT01 selected IPv6, member `eth1` and node `eth2`; AT08 selected IPv4 on `eth0`. Both ends' route, source, neighbour and WireGuard views are retained, and no success is attributed to a merge.\n- **AT02, under D-157:** one closed recovery. Closed Apply 544, then a renewal request 63.9 ms after the closed end, a populated generation 15 lease, and serving Apply 550, with one intervening request and no baseline write. **Deny-all 179 ms with 7 losses,** against 205 ms and 8 in run `3eb3960d`. D-157 is in both runs, so no timing change is attributed to a merge.\n- **AT09:** index 25 is blocked, not exercised: no grant-less lease followed the restart, so D-067's provisional path did not run. Index 26 passes, serving in 6.02 s with the first counted byte at 13.37 s. Index 27 passes: no `TC_FOREIGN_FILTER`.\n- **Agent restarts:** no `baseline_unverified` followed by `GENERATION_MISMATCH`, so F48-01's signature did not recur.\n- **Node writes:** 30, every one a first-attempt success with HTTP 202. Zero conflicts.\n- **Requests, routed by the orchestrator.**\n  - **Devstack (F22-D146):** the fixture cadence. The regular node reports every 30 s against the members predicate's 15 s bound. The lane changed neither, and kept the predicate. This goes to devstack's next follow-up.\n  - **Agent-core:** per-attempt observation submission logging. Neither `node/agent/observe.go` nor `node/internal/controlclient/client.go` logs an attempt's time or outcome, so the export cannot tell scheduling, queueing, transport and rejection apart. This goes to agent-core's next follow-up.\n  - **The D-148 owner:** F22-AT01's new evidence. F11-01 stays open.\n"
